From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=9C=A0=ED=98=84=EC=84=9D?= <evermongwan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:35:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lwipUDP: free the pbuf after a successful udp_sendto()

udp_sendto() does not take ownership of the pbuf. endPacket() dropped its
pointer on success without pbuf_free(), so every sent datagram leaked one
pbuf and UDP sending stopped once the pool was exhausted (seen on a
Portenta C33 after ~110 packets while Wi-Fi still reported connected).

Found during hardware testing of the UWB + Wi-Fi coexistence work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A3m3TFiwD564ej3SMfu7jv
---
 libraries/lwIpWrapper/src/lwipUDP.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libraries/lwIpWrapper/src/lwipUDP.cpp b/libraries/lwIpWrapper/src/lwipUDP.cpp
index 22f615d..ff1fa79 100644
--- a/libraries/lwIpWrapper/src/lwipUDP.cpp
+++ b/libraries/lwIpWrapper/src/lwipUDP.cpp
@@ -160,6 +160,12 @@ int lwipUDP::endPacket()
         return 0;
     }
 
+    /* udp_sendto() does not take ownership of the pbuf: release our
+       reference, otherwise every packet leaks one pbuf and sending stops
+       once the pool is exhausted (~110 packets on the C33). */
+    __disable_irq();
+    pbuf_free(_data);
+    __enable_irq();
     _data = NULL;
 
     CLwipIf::getInstance().lwip_task();
